-Remove the tile baseboard. -Open walls from the ground up 2 to 3 feet high for all wet walls. -Remove all wet insulation. -Install Air movers and dehumidifiers for 2 or 3 days. (Air movers help to ventilate the affected area, circulate air so that the moisture can be extracted by dehumidifiers and dry damp materials such as drywall and floors). -Install new insulation -Install new sheetrock and apply new plaster. -Install new tile baseboard. -Paint all walls.
